WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.290
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.210
Now, Pikachu!

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.720
Let’s go, Hibunny!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.250
Oh? We can hear passionate cries
in the institute today.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.670
Lightning Speed!

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.010
Well done, Go!

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.190
Hibunny!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.850
What is Hihidaruma doing?

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.450
Looks like it’s gonna do something!

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.090
Is it telling Hibunny to
use a Fire move, too?

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:52.050
PocketMonsters

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.470
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.050
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.770
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.640
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.980
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.650
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:12.150
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:17.410
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.000
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.920
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:31.670
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:38.680
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.890
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.230
Let's have a fight!

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.940
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.770
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.110
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.780
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.120
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.620
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.750
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.550
I choose you!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:22.560
Working For Tomorrow!!
Hibunny's Fiery Kick!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.430
Go! Satoshi!

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.270
You still haven’t had breakfast?

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.620
Barrierd was worried about you.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.040
What are you doing?

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.440
Oh, well, you see…

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.700
Huh…? Why does Hihidaruma
look so smug?

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:52.290
Hihidaruma provoked Hibunny
into trying to use Ember,

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.210
but it can’t really pull it off…

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.560
Hang in there, Hibunny!

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:58.650
Try more like…

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.730
<i>Graaaah!</i> Open up wide,

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.480
then launch the heat
from your belly, like, “<i>Ba-Ba-Ba-Bang!</i> ”

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.810
Yeah, that’s it!

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.890
What’s that mean?

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.930
I’m pretty sure that’s how Satoshi
tries to teach others…

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:13.470
But...

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.190
I don’t think there’s any need
to try so hard, though.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.490
You should stop.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.470
That’s enough.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.620
Stop, Hibunny!

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.440
Your Lightning Speed and Double Kick
have gotten really strong.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.970
It doesn’t matter if
you can’t use a Fire move.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:48.270
It seems Hibunny
doesn’t agree with you.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.780
Well…

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.810
You can’t do
what you can’t do.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.220
Hey!

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.910
Time for breakfast!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.650
Go, you’re heading into the city
to catch Pokémon today, right?

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.420
Yeah.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.960
Is catching Pokémon fun?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.960
It’s super fun!

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.010
You should come with us!

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.760
No thanks.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.140
Come on!

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.000
I told you no!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.780
Why not? It’s fun.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:35.350
Wait… Hibunny?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.340
Don’t worry!
It’ll come right back once it gets hungry.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.250
I guess.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.860
Hibunny!

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:06.800
See?

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.040
Thank goodness!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.670
All right, let’s go
catch some Pokémon!

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:15.030
I can’t wait to see
what kind of Pokémon we’ll find!

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.100
Me neither!

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.130
There’s nothing around!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:46.900
I thought we’d find at least a Poppo
or something right off the bat.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.760
What is it, Hibunny?

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.120
Hang on.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.730
I’m looking up what Pokémon
are in this area.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.120
Pelipper?!

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.840
What are you doing,
Hibunny?!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.230
After it!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.800
I can’t believe we found
a wild Pelipper…

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.770
We <i>gotta</i>  catch it!

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.450
Do you have <i>the thing?</i>

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:17.980
Indeed I do!

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:23.140
Kuchiba City’s limited-edition
sea-breeze flavor potato chips!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.580
Oh, yeah! That’s the stuff!

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.480
Let’s get right to it!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.010
<i>Time for some snacks!</i>

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.490
Oh, man…
I ate way too much.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.940
I need a break…

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.020
I got heartburn…

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.710
That’s a great idea, meow!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:43.990
What?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.290
Sonansu suggested we play
Nasty Plot Shiritori!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.340
Oh, great idea.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.300
Doing <i>nothing</i>
won’t do us any good!

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.150
Allow me to explain, meow.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:57.420
Nasty Plot Shiritori is Team Rocket’s very own,
original method of image training,

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.300
where we play Shiritori
using nothing but nasty phrases,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.060
so as to ensure that we’re
constantly thinking evil thoughts, meow!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.810
I’ll go first.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.730
Pitfall!
(otoshia<i>na</i>)

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.480
Knuckle punch!
(<i>na</i> kkuru pan<i>chi</i> )

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.850
Insidious punch!
(<i>go</i> kuaku pan<i>chi</i> )

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:14.580
Pure evil!
(<i>ch</i> ou gokuaku hido<i>u</i>)

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.000
Back-lying perpendicular armbar!
(<i>u</i> de hijiki juji gata<i>me</i>)

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.400
Bleeding gums!
(<i>ha</i> guki kara <i>chi</i> )

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:20.970
Chi...

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.250
Fatal wound!
(<i>chi</i> meisho<i>u</i> )

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.020
U… U… U…

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.340
Time out for a sec!

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.770
It just occurred to me,
Nyarth…

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.640
Are you <i>actually</i>  following up
on what Sonansu’s saying?

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.820
You ask that <i>now?</i>

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.420
You are, right, Nyarth?

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.720
Of course, meow!

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.120
Oh. Well, okay then.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:42.290
Right, it was my turn…

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.470
U… U… U…

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.600
Back fist!
(<i>u</i> rake<i>n</i> )

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:51.290
Oh, hold it!
Never mind what I just said!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.360
No go! You <i>totally</i>  had an “N”
at the end, there, meow!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.040
You lose, meow!

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.310
You definitely said “uraken”.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.540
No way!
I did <i>not</i> say “uraken”!

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.770
What I said was “ura<i>ke </i>”!
(Back hair)

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.810
“urake”? Is that even a thing?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.830
Yeah, it’s the…
hair in the back!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.180
I’ve never heard of that, meow!

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.800
What kind of hair?
In the back of <i>what?!</i>

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.300
You don’t know?!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:19.230
You know, eyelashes, eyebrows and back hair…
It’s all the rage these days!

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.100
There’s no way!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.250
S-Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up! Shut up!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.520
She’s gotten violent!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.850
Back hair is…
it’s <i>this</i>  hair here, got it?!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.650
We lost it.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.820
I just don’t have
any catching luck today…

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.050
What’s this?

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.790
What? What?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.560
What are you doing, meow?

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.400
Hey, don’t push!

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.890
You’re holding up the line,
so hurry up, meow!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.330
T-Team Rocket?!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.610
You’re the brat boy’s friend…
Brat boy Mk. II!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.000
Where?! Where is he, meow?!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.900
Hey, stop pushing!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:22.000
Well… For starters…
Let’s get out!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.870
W-Why’d you come out
from under that box?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:32.400
I-It’s not a <i>box!</i>
It’s a phone booth!

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.800
Phone? Booth?

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.520
He doesn’t know, meow!

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.780
Kids these days don’t know
what phone booths are, meow!

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:41.370
I told you, didn’t I?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.430
This is <i>way</i>  too conspicuous an
entrance to our base.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.020
What?! You’ve got
a base under here?!

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.890
Why, where ever did you
get <i>that</i> from?!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:52.200
It’s too late now, Kojiro…

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.150
Let’s get him!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.650
Yeah!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:57.120
Vending, come on!

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:01.470
Huh?

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.780
Nothing’s coming…

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.890
From <i>there?!</i>

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.160
The Pelipper from before!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.310
Which means that
this place getting exposed…

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:22.430
<i>…was Pelipper’s fault!</i>

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.800
Hey! Don’t run away!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.810
Go!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.280
Brat boy!

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:33.720
And…

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.060
Pikachu, meow!

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.830
You okay?

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:37.480
Yeah.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.300
All right, this is perfect!
Like a Pikachu to a flame!

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:42.290
Yeah!

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:43.820
Nyarth!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:45.280
Yeah, meow!

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:46.950
Rocket…

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.190
Vending…

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.780
Secret!

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:53.090
You’re up!

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:54.420
Come forth!

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:00.750
The Tadpole Pokémon,
Nyorobon!

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.510
The Snapping Pokémon,
Kamukame, meow!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.760
You’re the thing
from the other day!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.600
That thing that’s supposed to
get really strong when it evolves!

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:16.120
Hey… Can this baby even fight?

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.200
It’s saying “Bring it on!”, meow.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.780
For real?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.280
It doesn’t <i>look</i> strong, though…

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.280
But we can’t let this chance
go to waste!

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:27.910
Right!

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:30.310
Nyorobon! Water Gun!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.660
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:42.130
Kamukamu! Water Gun!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.550
Oh, wow!
That’s pretty impressive!

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.220
Hibunny! Dodge and
use Double Kick!

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:52.870
Hibunny!

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.830
Why Ember?!

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.440
PocketMonsters

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.130
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:08.530
PocketMonsters

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:13.450
.  Fire  .
Hihidaruma
PocketMonsters

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.240
Hibunny! Dodge and
use Double Kick!

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.630
Hibunny!

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.860
Why Ember?!

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:30.850
Hibunny!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.510
Well done, Kamukamu!

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:41.670
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.370
We almost had them that time!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.540
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.570
Hibunny!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.090
That Kamukame
was really strong.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.310
Yeah…

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.880
Are you okay, Hibunny?

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:14.880
Say, Hibunny…

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.530
Why did you use Ember
instead of Double Kick back there?

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.980
Didn’t I tell you?

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.730
You should focus on the moves
you can actually use,

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:32.300
and fight in a way that’s true to yourself.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:40.370
I told you, you don’t have…

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.330
Listen to me!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.340
That just isn’t good enough!

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.800
Ow!

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:56.160
Just accept that
there’s some things you <i>can’t</i>  do!

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.660
Oh, what now?

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.810
Fine, then! Have it your way.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.400
Hibunny!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.680
Go, you're not gonna follow it?

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.070
No.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.510
What’s gotten into it?!

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:18.970
I tried so hard to bring out
Hibunny’s strength in battle.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.850
Really?

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:22.670
Yeah!

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.380
Oh, I see.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.920
But that battle was,
how do I put it…

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:30.420
You and Hibunny
really weren’t one.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.720
“One”?

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:38.220
Yeah! Like how when Pikachu and I battle,
it’s like we merge into one being!

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.880
And then it’s like our chest
starts boiling and blazing up…

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.000
and we go all “<i>Ba-Ba-Ba-Bang!</i> ”

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.770
I have no idea what you mean…

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:52.610
Then you’ve gotta stick
with Hibunny until you <i>do</i>  get it!

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:54.240
Ow!

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.040
Where could Hibunny have gone?

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:28.610
Hibunny is dead-set on
using a Fire move, huh?

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.370
Hibunny!

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.200
That was…

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.790
Hey, wait, Hibunny!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.210
Ow!

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.710
Hey, you!
Watch where you’re…

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:55.280
<i>You again!</i>

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.720
Team Rocket!

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:57.960
Again!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.100
Second Pikachu encounter
of the day, meow!

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:04.710
This time, we <i>will</i>
get your Pikachu!

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:08.020
Kamukamu!
Use your Bite attack!

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.770
Dodge it, Hibunny!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:13.650
Hibunny!

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:18.280
There might be a Fire move
you <i>can</i>  use.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.780
This time, we’ll win for sure!

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:25.990
Let’s do it!

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:28.370
Lightning Speed!

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:31.120
Kamukamu! Headbutt!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:37.930
Are you okay?!

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:41.300
All right!
Use Double Kick!

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.600
Another Bite attack!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.810
Here they come!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.190
It dodged again!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:53.020
Double Kick!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:57.650
Kamukame?!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:06.290
We’re fighting as one…
Going all “<i>Ba-Ba-Ba-Bang!</i> ”…

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:09.790
I’ve never felt this way before.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:12.770
Hibunny!

